WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.821 --> 00:00:04.654
- Um, Luke.

00:00:04.654 --> 00:00:05.984
Okay, Luke has been asking this question

00:00:05.984 --> 00:00:07.577
at least ten times in the chat.

00:00:07.577 --> 00:00:09.048
Luke, I'm hearing you.

00:00:09.048 --> 00:00:11.075
There's a ton of questions,
we're going to get it.

00:00:11.075 --> 00:00:13.184
This is for you Luke, okay.

00:00:13.184 --> 00:00:16.077
Luke says I'm a young entrepreneur

00:00:16.077 --> 00:00:18.579
and people keep telling me
or giving me the feeling

00:00:18.579 --> 00:00:20.717
that I won't be successful.

00:00:20.717 --> 00:00:23.329
What advice do you have?

00:00:23.329 --> 00:00:24.318
- Wow, Luke.

00:00:24.318 --> 00:00:26.790
Actually I'll say one
thing that blew me away,

00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:29.479
I went on the floor and
we did loads of mentoring,

00:00:29.479 --> 00:00:33.646
I met a 14 year old entrepreneur
on a second business idea.

00:00:34.995 --> 00:00:37.330
I loved it, it blew me away.

00:00:37.330 --> 00:00:38.236
God.

00:00:38.236 --> 00:00:41.456
So Luke, I don't know what age you are

00:00:41.456 --> 00:00:43.706
but there is so many people

00:00:45.932 --> 00:00:49.432
and maybe this is a little bit agist

00:00:49.432 --> 00:00:52.590
but particularly some older people

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:55.121
who probably will tell you the reasons

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:57.181
why it's not such a good idea.

00:00:57.181 --> 00:00:58.512
But if you believe in it

00:00:58.512 --> 00:01:01.125
and then do everything we talked
about in previous programs,

00:01:01.125 --> 00:01:04.670
test your idea, test
drive it, road test it,

00:01:04.670 --> 00:01:07.263
you can road test it with your friends,

00:01:07.263 --> 00:01:09.514
you can road test it on social,

00:01:09.514 --> 00:01:11.119
and you can create a following,

00:01:11.119 --> 00:01:14.159
and that will give you
the energy and positivity

00:01:14.159 --> 00:01:16.484
to know that your idea's going to land.

00:01:16.484 --> 00:01:18.570
But how do you know if an idea

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:21.429
is not going to land if you don't try it.

00:01:21.429 --> 00:01:24.884
And back to that example,
if you don't try it,

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:26.978
you know failure is
actually, not trying it.

00:01:26.978 --> 00:01:30.963
The fear of failure actually creates it,

00:01:30.963 --> 00:01:32.908
it's almost like a cancer,
you fail to try it,

00:01:32.908 --> 00:01:37.050
then you've let us all down
because you could've done it.

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:39.311
I'll tell you, Evan will tell you today,

00:01:39.311 --> 00:01:42.675
if you have an idea, if you back yourself,

00:01:42.675 --> 00:01:44.425
you're halfway there.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:47.253
And what is brilliant

00:01:47.253 --> 00:01:49.595
and what I love doing more than anything

00:01:49.595 --> 00:01:51.445
is defying the cynics.

00:01:51.445 --> 00:01:55.685
Loads of people could
be cynical or jealous.

00:01:55.685 --> 00:01:58.037
People might be jealous
that you've had that idea,

00:01:58.037 --> 00:02:01.135
and you're going to make
your idea come to reality.

00:02:01.135 --> 00:02:04.114
And you're going to make
your dreams come true.

00:02:04.114 --> 00:02:06.931
But back yourself, and I...

00:02:06.931 --> 00:02:10.643
Whatever happens, you
know, and it's amazing,

00:02:10.643 --> 00:02:12.433
you never know what twists and turns

00:02:12.433 --> 00:02:13.776
life's got in front of you.

00:02:13.776 --> 00:02:14.801
So I'll give you an example,

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:17.134
when I left graduate school,

00:02:17.982 --> 00:02:19.896
and it was before the internet,

00:02:19.896 --> 00:02:23.857
so I wrote, one of my buddies,
I'll give you an example,

00:02:23.857 --> 00:02:26.398
a real good buddy called
Paul Smith, great guy,

00:02:26.398 --> 00:02:28.963
he wrote 240 companies,

00:02:28.963 --> 00:02:32.297
240 companies.

00:02:32.297 --> 00:02:35.512
And he only got a handful of replies,

00:02:35.512 --> 00:02:37.230
all of those turned him down,

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:38.722
he didn't even get an interview.

00:02:38.722 --> 00:02:41.256
But he kept on going and just,

00:02:41.256 --> 00:02:43.401
can you imagine how demoralizing.

00:02:43.401 --> 00:02:46.864
I got turned down by so many
companies for graduate school.

00:02:46.864 --> 00:02:48.292
I even got turned down,

00:02:48.292 --> 00:02:50.873
you know I applied to all these
great companies at the top

00:02:50.873 --> 00:02:54.373
called Unilever, and all these great, PNG,

00:02:55.934 --> 00:02:57.322
and they turned me down.

00:02:57.322 --> 00:02:59.942
So one of the things, funny thing is,

00:02:59.942 --> 00:03:02.961
Evan, in those days you kind
of did these placements.

00:03:02.961 --> 00:03:05.693
I did a four year course
and I did kind of two,

00:03:05.693 --> 00:03:09.033
they call it sandwich course,
a placement of the company.

00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:11.544
And the company that I
did a placement at, BP,

00:03:11.544 --> 00:03:13.701
I thought I was a shoe-in for the job,

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:17.494
I went for the job, and I got turned down!

00:03:17.494 --> 00:03:19.628
How does that work?

00:03:19.628 --> 00:03:22.440
But you just got to pick yourself up

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:24.947
what what I would say,
there's a few things,

00:03:24.947 --> 00:03:26.577
in that sort of scenario,

00:03:26.577 --> 00:03:31.375
one of the things that I
ask for which is so powerful

00:03:31.375 --> 00:03:34.099
that I don't think very
few people ask for,

00:03:34.099 --> 00:03:37.559
is a magic word called feedback.

00:03:37.559 --> 00:03:39.642
If people turn you down,

00:03:39.642 --> 00:03:42.348
whether it's for an audition
if you want to be an actor,

00:03:42.348 --> 00:03:46.103
whether it's a business
person, you did a pitch,

00:03:46.103 --> 00:03:48.318
or if you're going to
lay the stage company,

00:03:48.318 --> 00:03:49.611
if you're going to raise money

00:03:49.611 --> 00:03:52.492
and you do a pitch to your family,

00:03:52.492 --> 00:03:54.791
why they backed you and
why they turned you down.

00:03:54.791 --> 00:03:57.816
If you ask for feedback,
it is mind-blowing

00:03:57.816 --> 00:04:02.316
how you can improve your
business, your product,

00:04:02.316 --> 00:04:04.902
your whole sales pitch, your web site,

00:04:04.902 --> 00:04:06.581
your social experience.

00:04:06.581 --> 00:04:09.356
So I think, bottom line Luke,

00:04:09.356 --> 00:04:13.439
is back yourself, defy
the cynics, try your idea,

00:04:15.541 --> 00:04:17.692
and constantly have
those social antenna on,

00:04:17.692 --> 00:04:21.883
to say how can I constantly
improve and create my product,

00:04:21.883 --> 00:04:25.807
and my idea to make it
land and make it big.

00:04:25.807 --> 00:04:26.926
- I love it.

00:04:26.926 --> 00:04:28.974
And Luke is loving that
we picked his question,

00:04:28.974 --> 00:04:31.141
so he's happy in the chat.

00:04:32.915 --> 00:04:34.934
Luke, I would say,

00:04:34.934 --> 00:04:37.759
I would say, one, back to our
initial comment at the top,

00:04:37.759 --> 00:04:39.936
about the environment,
the environment matters.

00:04:39.936 --> 00:04:41.756
I would start surrounding myself with

00:04:41.756 --> 00:04:44.184
young entrepreneurs who are
off trying to do something.

00:04:44.184 --> 00:04:47.156
And if you don't have any young
entrepreneurs that you know,

00:04:47.156 --> 00:04:50.127
go to meetups, go to events,
try to connect with them.

00:04:50.127 --> 00:04:52.061
If you still can't find them,

00:04:52.061 --> 00:04:54.511
then read articles, watch videos,

00:04:54.511 --> 00:04:56.361
learn from people who are already doing it

00:04:56.361 --> 00:04:59.334
so that you know that if it's possible.

00:04:59.334 --> 00:05:02.017
I think Mark Zuckerberg's
big success made it possible

00:05:02.017 --> 00:05:04.018
for a lot of young
entrepreneurs to realize

00:05:04.018 --> 00:05:05.469
hey if he can do it, I can do it too,

00:05:05.469 --> 00:05:08.210
I'm going to bet on myself.

00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:10.586
And then the second thing
I would think about is

00:05:10.586 --> 00:05:12.405
the people who are giving you the advice,

00:05:12.405 --> 00:05:13.593
and maybe because they're jealous,

00:05:13.593 --> 00:05:14.993
and maybe because they love you.

00:05:14.993 --> 00:05:16.280
Maybe mom and dad love you

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:19.283
and they just don't want to see you fail.

00:05:19.283 --> 00:05:20.304
They're not trying to hurt you,

00:05:20.304 --> 00:05:22.959
they think they're trying to help you.

00:05:22.959 --> 00:05:25.126
I would look at, have the people

00:05:25.126 --> 00:05:27.412
who are giving you this
advice done it before?

00:05:27.412 --> 00:05:30.214
Have they done it themselves?

00:05:30.214 --> 00:05:32.500
If they haven't, then they may
not be in the best position,

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:34.369
like the people who are hating on you,

00:05:34.369 --> 00:05:35.202
if they haven't done it themselves,

00:05:35.202 --> 00:05:36.371
they haven't taken a chance themselves,

00:05:36.371 --> 00:05:37.204
maybe they're not the best people

00:05:37.204 --> 00:05:39.872
to kind of be giving you that advice.

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:41.273
So I wouldn't pay
attention to them, right?

00:05:41.273 --> 00:05:45.440
Find out, seek out the mentors
who you can learn from.

